<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="dimension-properties">
    <title>Dimension properties</title>
    <shortdesc>This reference lists the <xref href="../glossaries/CSS.dita">CSS</xref> sizing properties documented in <xref keyref="ch-box-dimensions">Box dimensions</xref>. The <codeph>Values</codeph> column gives CSS syntax.</shortdesc>
    <!-- TODO: fill the Default cells and describe how each property affects layout in the PDF -->
    <refbody>
        <section>
            <p>CSS Anchor Positioning permits <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph> only on properties accepted in an <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-anchor-position-1/#accepted-position-try-properties" scope="external" format="html">
                    <codeph>@position-try</codeph> rule</xref>. These include sizing, inset, and margin properties. This page lists the sizing properties.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="preferred-sizes">
            <title>Preferred sizes</title>
            <table id="dimension-properties__I_1n_">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <colspec colname="c1" />
                    <colspec colname="c2" />
                    <colspec colname="c3" />
                    <colspec colname="c4" />
                    <colspec colname="c5" />
                    <thead>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry align="center">Name</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Description</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Values</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Default</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Specification</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-width" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>width</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred physical width.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-width" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-height" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>height</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred physical height.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-height" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>inline-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred size on the inline axis.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-block-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>block-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred size on the block axis.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-block-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph> means a length such as <codeph>12pt</codeph>, a percentage such as <codeph>60%</codeph>, or a <codeph>calc()</codeph> expression combining them.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <codeph>[0,∞]</codeph> in <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph> means the length or percentage cannot be negative.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-anchor-position-1/#funcdef-anchor-size" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>
                        </xref> accepts an optional anchor name, an optional size keyword, or both, followed by an optional length or percentage fallback. It resolves to the anchor’s size only when the box is absolutely positioned and has a target anchor. Otherwise, it resolves to the fallback. Without a fallback, the declaration becomes invalid at computed-value time. The sizing properties listed here include physical and logical properties.</p>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </section>
