                                <codeph>none</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-block-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph> means a length such as <codeph>12pt</codeph>, a percentage such as <codeph>60%</codeph>, or a <codeph>calc()</codeph> expression combining them.</li>
                <li>
                    <codeph>[0,∞]</codeph> in <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph> means the length or percentage cannot be negative.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section id="paired-size-shorthands">
            <title>Paired size shorthands</title>
            <table id="dimension-properties__I_1r_">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <colspec colname="c1" />
                    <colspec colname="c2" />
                    <colspec colname="c3" />
                    <colspec colname="c4" />
                    <colspec colname="c5" />
                    <thead>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry align="center">Name</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Description</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Values</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Default</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Specification</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets <codeph>width</codeph> and <codeph>height</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">One or two preferred-size values.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-min-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>min-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets <codeph>min-width</codeph> and <codeph>min-height</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">One or two minimum-size values.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-min-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-max-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>max-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets <codeph>max-width</codeph> and <codeph>max-height</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">One or two maximum-size values.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-max-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <ul>
                <li>Each pair takes the corresponding longhand’s values in width-then-height order. The second value is optional and defaults to the first.</li>
                <li>The <codeph>size</codeph> shorthand is not valid in an <codeph>@page</codeph> context. That context has a separate <codeph>size</codeph> descriptor for page dimensions.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section id="aspect-ratio-and-intrinsic-sizes">
            <title>Aspect ratio and intrinsic sizes</title>
            <table id="dimension-properties__I_1t_">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <colspec colname="c1" />
                    <colspec colname="c2" />
                    <colspec colname="c3" />
                    <colspec colname="c4" />
                    <colspec colname="c5" />
                    <thead>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry align="center">Name</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Description</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Values</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Default</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Specification</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-aspect-ratio" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>aspect-ratio</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Supplies a preferred ratio between the width and height.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, a non-negative number such as <codeph>1.5</codeph>, or two non-negative numbers such as <codeph>16 / 9</codeph>; <codeph>auto</codeph> can be combined with a number.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-aspect-ratio" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-width" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>contain-intrinsic-width</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Fallback intrinsic width under size containment.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">Optional <codeph>auto</codeph>; <codeph>none</codeph> or a non-negative length.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-width" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-height" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>contain-intrinsic-height</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Fallback intrinsic height under size containment.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">Optional <codeph>auto</codeph>; <codeph>none</codeph> or a non-negative length.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-height" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>contain-intrinsic-inline-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Fallback intrinsic inline size under size containment.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">Optional <codeph>auto</codeph>; <codeph>none</codeph> or a non-negative length.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-block-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>contain-intrinsic-block-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Fallback intrinsic block size under size containment.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">Optional <codeph>auto</codeph>; <codeph>none</codeph> or a non-negative length.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-block-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>contain-intrinsic-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets fallback intrinsic width and height.</entry>
                            <entry namest="c3" nameend="c4">One or two longhand values; see below.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-contain-intrinsic-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <ul>
                <li>For <codeph>aspect-ratio</codeph>, the first number is the width and the second is the height. If you give one number, the second number is <codeph>1</codeph>. For example, <codeph>1.5</codeph> means the same ratio as <codeph>1.5 / 1</codeph>.</li>
                <li>Each <codeph>contain-intrinsic-*</codeph> longhand accepts an optional <codeph>auto</codeph>, followed by <codeph>none</codeph> or a non-negative length.</li>
                <li>The <codeph>contain-intrinsic-size</codeph> shorthand takes one or two such values. One value applies to both dimensions.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section id="replaced-elements-and-intrinsic-contributions">
            <title>Replaced elements and intrinsic contributions</title>
            <table id="dimension-properties__I_1v_">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <colspec colname="c1" />
                    <colspec colname="c2" />
                    <colspec colname="c3" />
                    <colspec colname="c4" />
                    <colspec colname="c5" />
                    <thead>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry align="center">Name</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Description</entry>
